From b343ad54e6c9ac346abed9cddfd30a5387c34d13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:16:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): lanes third review: the CLI decides who is a
 person; outages keep the last policy [daveey]

- hermes kanban create keeps the user/dashboard labels only for a typed slash command or a human shell, and
  stores agent otherwise (lanes configured only); creation no longer guesses from the environment
- a worker card behind the call counts only in the dispatcher-owned worker context
- an unreadable config keeps the last policy this process read, so an outage does not open the gate
- held excludes cards the sweep or decompose released; lanes held --lane filters by the lane a card counts in
- an agent's CLI admit spends the daily budget; delegated children cannot run lanes
- lane_tenant applies the board's project and workdir defaults as creation does

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
